{"name":"Kilimanjaro","hex":"#3a3532","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Kilimanjaro","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A volcano in Tanzania, the highest peak in Africa at 5,895 meters (19,321 feet)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Kilimanjaro"}],"entries":[{"title":"Kilimanjaro (The Teardrop Explodes album)","blocks":[{"text":"Kilimanjaro is the debut album by the neo-psychedelic Liverpool band The Teardrop Explodes, released on 10 October 1980. It contains versions of the band's early singles \"Sleeping Gas\", \"Bouncing Babies\", \"Treason\" and \"When I Dream\"; reissues of the album also include their biggest hit, \"Reward\". The album also includes the song \"Books\", originally a song by Julian Cope's previous band, The Crucial Three; it was also recorded by Echo & the Bunnymen. In 2000, Q magazine placed Kilimanjaro at number 95 in its list of the \"100 Greatest British Albums Ever\"."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/d/d4/Teardrop_Explodes_-_Kilimanjaro_CD_album_cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kilimanjaro_(The_Teardrop_Explodes_album)","wikidata":"Q265406"},{"title":"Kilimanjaro (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Kilimanjaro\" is a Tamil song from the 2010 Indian film Enthiran, directed by S. Shankar. The song was composed by A. R. Rahman, lyrics penned by Pa.Vijay and sung by Javed Ali and Chinmayi. The Hindi and Telugu version of the song has lyrics respectively written by Swanand Kirkire and Bhuvana Chandra. The song, based on the raga Karaharapriya, is reputed for its use of tribal beats with a catchy chorus and with various musical experiments. Song shooting took place in Machu Picchu in Peru. The song was released in Hindi and Telugu under the same name."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5b/Kilimanjarosong.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kilimanjaro_(song)","wikidata":"Q6406943"},{"title":"Mount Kilimanjaro","blocks":[{"text":"Mount Kilimanjaro is a large dormant stratovolcano in Tanzania. It is the highest mountain in Africa and the highest free-standing mountain above sea level in the world, at 5,895 m (19,341 ft) above sea level and 4,900 m (16,100 ft) above its plateau base. It is also the highest volcano in the Eastern Hemisphere and the fourth most prominent peak on Earth."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Kilimanjaro_from_Amboseli.jpg/330px-Kilimanjaro_from_Amboseli.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mount_Kilimanjaro","wikidata":"Q7296"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c3/The_Teardrop_Explodes_-_Kilimanjaro_.jpg/250px-The_Teardrop_Explodes_-_Kilimanjaro_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/c/c3/The_Teardrop_Explodes_-_Kilimanjaro_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c3/The_Teardrop_Explodes_-_Kilimanjaro_.jpg/250px-The_Teardrop_Explodes_-_Kilimanjaro_.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Teardrop_Explodes_-_Kilimanjaro_.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/The_Kibo_and_Mawenzi_Cones_of_Mt._Kilimanjaro.jpg/500px-The_Kibo_and_Mawenzi_Cones_of_Mt._Kilimanjaro.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/The_Kibo_and_Mawenzi_Cones_of_Mt._Kilimanjaro.jpg/500px-The_Kibo_and_Mawenzi_Cones_of_Mt._Kilimanjaro.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail",